{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"unadhesive-caloric-sapsucker","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\n`__main__.main()` (`:506-670`) runs the guard sequence — pause (`:566`), lock-file purge (`:575`), pass-lock check/steal/acquire (`:588-630`), heartbeat + `abort_check` (`:631-642`), `last_pass.finalize_process`/`release_process_lock` (`:657-668`) — but `_lib_ops._bridge_run` (`:213-248`) calls `run_pass_result` (`:346`) directly. MCP `bridge_sync` (`_mcp_reads.py:85-99` → `rebar.bridge_sync`) therefore runs an unlocked, un-heartbeated, unpublished live pass that ignores the pause ref. This story is a bug fix. Cites are on origin/main 083620b0 (engine paths are under `src/rebar/reconciler/` after the package move).\n\n## Approach\n1. New module `src/rebar/reconciler/guarded_pass.py` moves `_Disposition`, `PassResult`, `run_pass_result`, `_reconcile_exception_result`, `_optional_request_kwargs`, `_project_visibility_preflight`, `_pause_exit_code` (renamed `_pause_result`), `_post_pause_preflight`, `_resolve_request_selection` out of `__main__.py` and exports `def run_guarded_pass(request: ReconcileRequest, *, advisory=None) -> PassResult`.\n2. Semantics, order fixed: (1) `route == \"preview\"` → no guards, return `run_pass_result(...)`; (2) resolve `request.selection_tokens` → on `SelectionError` return `PassResult(INVALID_INVOCATION, {\"error\": msg}, legacy_message=f\"ERROR: {msg}\")`; (3) pause → `PassResult(PAUSED, status, legacy_message=marker, canonical_message=marker)`, corrupt gate → `OPERATIONAL_FAILURE`; (4) `_purge_committed_reconciler_locks` when unscoped; (5) `pass_id`; (6) `_post_pause_preflight` → `IN_FLIGHT`/`PHASE_GATE` with today's legacy messages; (7) `_resolve_held_lock` → `IN_FLIGHT` \"held by a live pass — yielding\"; (8) acquire/adopt, `Heartbeat`, `abort_check`, run `run_pass_result(...)` under `last_pass.finalize_process`, release in `finally`; any acquire/heartbeat exception → `PassResult(OPERATIONAL_FAILURE, {\"error\": str(exc)}, legacy_message=\"ERROR: reconciler process failed before finalization: …\")`. `run_guarded_pass` prints nothing to stdout.\n3. `last_pass.finalize_process` changes to `(repo_root, pass_id, run: Callable[[], PassResult]) -> PassResult` and publishes from the disposition (`RESCHEDULE` → `\"reschedule\"`, `OPERATIONAL_FAILURE` and `INVALID_INVOCATION` → `\"operational_failure\"`, exception → `\"exception\"`, `CONVERGED` and `PAUSED` → success). This removes the `exit_code == 75` sniff (`last_pass.py:376`) and fixes the latent route-dependence where a `sync` reschedule published `success`.\n4. `main()` keeps argv parsing, `_bind_operation_snapshot`, `_dry_run_enumeration_exit`, then `result = run_guarded_pass(request)` and renders via the existing `run_pass` print block + `_finish_disposition` (`run_pass` renamed `_render_pass(result, route) -> int`).\n5. `_lib_ops._bridge_run` builds `ReconcileRequest(route=…, repo_root=root, target_mode=Mode.DRY_RUN|LIVE, max_changes=…, selection_kind=…, selection_tokens=tuple(stripped only/exclude))`, calls `run_guarded_pass`, keeps `returncode = result.disposition.canonical_exit` and the `RebarError` mapping; `_bridge_selection` is deleted (`_validate_selection_args` stays). `_mcp_reads.bridge_sync` is unchanged (it already calls `rebar.bridge_sync`); `bridge_run.schema.json` already admits `paused`/`in-flight`. `_bridge_runner.py` imports `_Disposition` from `guarded_pass`.\n6. Docs: `docs/mcp-reference.md` (`bridge_sync` now honors pause and lock), `docs/concurrency.md` (one guard sequence for CLI, library, MCP).\n\nBREAKING: library/MCP `bridge_sync` now returns `state: paused|in-flight` (returncode 0) instead of running unguarded; a rescheduled `sync` pass publishes `failure_kind=reschedule` in `refs/reconciler/last-pass`.\n\n## Scope\n`src/rebar/reconciler/guarded_pass.py` (new, ~300 LOC), `src/rebar/reconciler/__main__.py`, `src/rebar/reconciler/last_pass.py`, `src/rebar/_lib_ops.py`, `src/rebar/_bridge_runner.py`, `tests/interfaces/store/test_bridge_sync_holds_ref_lock.py` (new), `tests/unit/reconciler/orchestrate/`, `docs/mcp-reference.md`, `docs/concurrency.md`. Out of scope: the runner's spawn chain (next story), `src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py`, `bridge_run.schema.json`, and the pass body itself (`reconcile_once`).\n\n## Testing\nHappy: new `tests/interfaces/store/test_bridge_sync_holds_ref_lock.py` — `git init` + `.tickets-tracker/.env-id` + tickets branch fixture (mirror `tests/unit/reconciler/orchestrate/test_main_entry.py::_git_repo`), monkeypatch `rebar.reconciler.reconcile.reconcile_once` with a stub that inside its body asserts `git rev-parse --verify refs/reconciler/lock` succeeds and `abort_check` is callable; after `rebar.bridge_sync()` returns, `refs/reconciler/lock` is absent and `refs/reconciler/last-pass` decodes to `outcome=success`. Edge: (a) pre-acquire the lock via `rebar.reconciler._ref_lock.acquire(repo, LOCK_REF, holder=\"other\", lease_secs=600)` → `bridge_sync()` returns `state==\"in-flight\"`, `returncode==0`, stub not called; (b) `rebar.bridge_pause(\"maint\")` first → `state==\"paused\"`, stub not called; (c) stub raises `RescheduleError` → `last-pass` shows `failure_kind==\"reschedule\"` for both `sync` and the CLI `--mode live` route; (d) existing `test_main_entry.py`/`test_reconcile_main.py` patch targets move to `rebar.reconciler.guarded_pass`; (e) `python -m rebar.reconciler sync` stdout/stderr contract tests (`tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_cli_heldout.py`) unchanged. Commands: `pytest tests/interfaces/store/test_bridge_sync_holds_ref_lock.py tests/unit/reconciler/orchestrate -q`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `git grep -n 'run_pass_result(' -- src` shows exactly one caller: `guarded_pass.run_guarded_pass`.\n- [ ] `rebar.bridge_sync()` observes `refs/reconciler/lock` held during the pass and released after — the new interfaces test.\n- [ ] `rebar.bridge_sync()` under an active pause returns `state==\"paused\"` without invoking `reconcile_once` — the new interfaces test, edge (b).\n- [ ] `last_pass.publish_process_result` has no `== 75` comparison — grep.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.","id":"f75f-5d85-7b9a-4d86","parent_id":"ebf5-5d21-0124-4313","priority":2,"tags":["complexity-reduction","breaking-pass-4"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Add run_guarded_pass as the one guarded core for the CLI, library and MCP bridge_sync"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788807415066488860,"uuid":"212ba50c-1be6-46d2-b926-9dde979b7691"}